WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.949 --> 00:00:06.359
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and since Robert
Kirkman and Scott Gimple have been talking

00:00:06.359 --> 00:00:10.120
about Season 5 and Negan I wanted to talk
with you about actors.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:12.769
I don’t know about you but I was really
surprised they confirmed he would be a thing

00:00:12.769 --> 00:00:13.769
this season.

00:00:13.769 --> 00:00:17.220
They were pretty vague about when and how
he’ll appear but we can pick apart the clues

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:18.460
in a sec.

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:26.420
Since this is kind of my first bonus video
for Season 5 I also want you guys to let me

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:29.410
know what kind of bonus Walking Dead vids
you’d like to see in the off season.

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:30.470
Just write your requests in the comments.

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:31.760
And be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:32.760
I think until I start doing youtube videos
full time I can only do about 1 a week average.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:36.750
So let’s get started with all the Negan
what not by asking a question?

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:39.880
What kind of an actor do we want?

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:44.910
Negan is without a doubt one of the worst
most casually sadistic people we’ve ever

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:46.010
read about.

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:48.489
Is there an actor out there that can pull
that off.

00:00:48.489 --> 00:00:53.489
When I made my Top 10 list I tried to focus
on actors that one, could outshine Andrew

00:00:53.489 --> 00:00:56.010
Lincoln and Norman Reedus if they were all
in a scene together, two someone that could

00:00:56.010 --> 00:01:00.920
convey the comedy of the character.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:05.390
As awful as Negan is, I always kind of felt
like we were meant to laugh at his cruel jokes

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:07.729
and then feel really awful about it.

00:01:07.729 --> 00:01:11.679
Like Kirkman wants you to treat Negan like
a sadistic comedian.

00:01:11.679 --> 00:01:15.899
So all these potential actors have to be imposing,
funny and super evil.

00:01:15.899 --> 00:01:18.189
Without looking like they’re doing an impression
of The Joker.

00:01:18.189 --> 00:01:23.759
Here’s the list Number 10 - Paying Homage
To Robert Kirkman’s Comments, Jon Hamm.

00:01:23.759 --> 00:01:28.689
So everyone asks Kirkman about Negan all the
time, and in a recent Interview he threw out

00:01:28.689 --> 00:01:31.850
Jon Hamm’s name as a solid choice for the
character.

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:37.499
Just because there is something of a physical
resemblance.

00:01:37.499 --> 00:01:41.360
Negan has those really strong features, jet
black hair and he’s super tall.

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:45.140
Just picture Don Draper really pissed off
with a baseball bat.

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:47.560
That he’s nicknamed Lucille.

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:55.249
The other reason he picked Jon Hamm has a
lot to do with the craziness inherent to the

00:01:55.249 --> 00:01:58.029
Negan Character.

00:01:58.029 --> 00:02:02.709
Any actor who plays the part will have to
be as crazy as the Joker, but be able to hold

00:02:02.709 --> 00:02:03.709
it in behind those crazy eyes you see in the
comic book.

00:02:03.709 --> 00:02:07.899
And Jon Hamm is a master of making you scared
just by staring at you.

00:02:07.899 --> 00:02:09.979
Number 9 - Henry Rollins

00:02:09.979 --> 00:02:14.780
There was this old Walking Dead Comic Con
2012 panel where the artist on the comic book,

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:18.680
Charlie Adlard said Negan was based on Henry
Rollins.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:20.840
Both in his look and intensity.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:25.190
I haven’t listened to Henry Rollins recently,
but even if you don’t know his music, just

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:27.680
check him out on Sons of Anarchy.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:32.819
Interesting side note, he also voiced a small
part in Batman Brave and the Bold and Adventure

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:33.819
Time.

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:34.819
As really intense cartoon characters.

00:02:34.819 --> 00:02:36.200
Number 8 - James Purefoy who’s actually
on The Following

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:41.200
He’s done some comic book material before
in Solomon Kane, but if he bulked up a little

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:44.680
bit and got more physical he could totally
pull of Negan.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:49.530
His villain on The Following is a little more
insidious than Negan.

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:54.319
Everyone has their own opinion on how Negan
expresses his evil.

00:02:54.319 --> 00:02:57.460
I always thought of his alignment as being
Lawful Evil.

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:00.939
Like he has his own code and rules that he
follows and if you break them, instead of

00:03:00.939 --> 00:03:02.219
kicking you out of the group.

00:03:02.219 --> 00:03:03.409
He’ll just slaughter you.

00:03:03.409 --> 00:03:06.760
There’s even a lot of father-son parallels
that come up.

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:11.370
And I think Purefoy could totally be a really
convincing evil father figure.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:14.769
Like Lucius Malfoy before Voldemort took control.

00:03:14.769 --> 00:03:17.359
Number 7 - Patrick Warburton

00:03:17.359 --> 00:03:20.719
Most people now know him as the voice of Joe
on Family Guy, but he’s essentially a comedic

00:03:20.719 --> 00:03:24.219
actor that mostly plays large imposing characters.

00:03:24.219 --> 00:03:27.100
He’d be perfect for the comedic aspects
of Negan.

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:28.950
Like the endless f-bombs he drops.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:31.959
He’s also really good at using his size
to be scary.

00:03:31.959 --> 00:03:35.859
I like the idea of Negan having Joe’s voice.

00:03:35.859 --> 00:03:38.819
But here’s a quick question I want you to
answer in the comments.

00:03:38.819 --> 00:03:42.640
What kind of a voice do you think Negan has?

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:45.480
Does he have that deep Family Guy Joe voice?

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:48.349
Or is it softer or more high pitched?

00:03:48.349 --> 00:03:51.450
I always read him as having a deep voice to
match his big body.

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:52.830
Number 6 - Michael Madsen

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:57.819
He’s the perfect mix of crazy and funny
too, so I had to put him on the list somewhere.

00:03:57.819 --> 00:04:02.240
Seriously, even in real life he’s like Gary
Busey, just a little bit crazy.

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:05.450
He’s a little older than I see the character
being, and he’d have to get in better shape.

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:09.799
But the show does fudge the way people look
sometimes if the actor is right for the part.

00:04:09.799 --> 00:04:14.040
David Morrissey didn’t look anything like
the comic book Governor.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:16.230
But he was such a great actor it totally worked.

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:19.950
I have a feeling Michael Madsen is one of
those actors that has to improvise everything,

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:24.700
so I think not being able to stick to the
script might be a problem.

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:27.910
When you’re adapting a comic that’s already
so good.

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:30.090
Changing a lot of the dialogue isn’t a good
idea.

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:33.130
Especially if you’re doing scenes right
off the page.

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:35.070
Number 5 - Nicolas Cage

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:39.070
Another crazy in real life actor that could
pull it off on the show.

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:45.720
Cage is still relatively sought after for
film roles, so his schedule might prevent

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:46.890
him from doing a series.

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:49.370
But if Negan isn’t featured too often it
could work.

00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:52.150
Supposedly the character will only have a
minor appearance this season.

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:54.120
He’d also have to bulk up a little bit,
but he’s close enough to the look that I

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:56.280
think if you ran into him late at night on
the street you might actually mistake him

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:58.970
for Negan.

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:00.570
Number 4 - Dominic West

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:03.470
He’d have to do it with an American accent.

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:07.810
I feel like you really need to see him on
The Wire as Jimmy Mcnulty to appreciate how

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:11.140
good he is at making you like a character
that’s awful.

00:05:11.140 --> 00:05:15.230
No one expects you to empathize with Negan,
but there are moments when we’re supposed

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:16.230
to root for him.

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:19.060
And that’s going to be one of the hardest
things for actors to do.

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:21.100
We have to root for a terrible human being.

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:23.220
Not all the time, but in the right moments.

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:26.880
A good example of an evil character that we’re
not supposed to root for is Joffrey on Game

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:27.880
Of Thrones.

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:28.880
The value proposition there is way simpler.

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:29.880
Hate his guts.

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:30.880
I think if they want Walking Dead Season 5
and 6 to be as successful as Season 4, we

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:31.880
have to be able to root for the villain every
once and a while.

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:32.880
And Dominic West is great at doing that.

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:34.860
Number 3 - Tamoh Penikett

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:38.990
Right now he’s doing a great job of playing
an evil angel on Supernatural.

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:42.120
Most people probably just remember him as
Helo from Battlestar.

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:46.370
But I’ve really enjoyed him more in the
bad guy roles he’s played since then.

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:52.110
He’s got the right look and physicality
for it, and as a performer, he won’t necessarily

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:56.130
outswing Andrew Lincoln, Norman Reedus or
any of the other main cast members when they

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:57.130
have to share screen time.

00:05:57.130 --> 00:05:58.130
You really want your characters to be equally
matched.

00:05:58.130 --> 00:06:03.470
It just makes it a lot more fun to watch when
it’s hard to tell who’s the biggest badass

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:04.470
in a scene.

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:07.770
And Season 5 is all about the return of badass
Rick.

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:12.360
I think the thing the thing that will make
Negan seem like an insurmountable obstacle

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:13.660
will be his gang.

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:19.010
He’s just one man, so if Daryl, Rick, Tyreese
and Abraham jumped him all at once he’d

00:06:19.010 --> 00:06:20.010
go down.

00:06:20.010 --> 00:06:21.240
But Negan has the Saviors.

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:24.220
He’s got his own evil version of the survivors.

00:06:24.220 --> 00:06:28.670
The other thing about Tamoh is that he’s
very attainable as a star.

00:06:28.670 --> 00:06:33.570
He’s not like a major A list star, so he’s
cheaper than say Nicolas Cage and probably

00:06:33.570 --> 00:06:37.400
more willing to play an iconic comic book
villain on a tv show.

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:41.030
Number 2 - Ray Stevenson

00:06:41.030 --> 00:06:46.250
He was a very very bloody version of The Punisher,
but imagine a cross between that character

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:48.250
and his character on Dexter.

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:50.270
Both psychopaths, just like Negan.

00:06:50.270 --> 00:06:53.960
But more balanced in terms of the amount of
dialogue and violence.

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:56.320
Negan talks a lot and The Punisher does not.

00:06:56.320 --> 00:07:03.930
He’s got all the physical requirements and
he’s an amazing actor.

00:07:03.930 --> 00:07:07.860
If you haven’t you should watch his season
of Dexter, it wasn’t the last one.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.110
I think it was Season 7.

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:12.720
He was one of the best villains that show
ever had.

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:19.620
And he can do that crazy over the top Punisher
level violence too.

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:22.050
Negan actually does go there a few times.

00:07:22.050 --> 00:07:25.610
Based on what Scott Gimple has said, Negan’s
appearance in Season 5 will be very brief.

00:07:25.610 --> 00:07:30.410
So I think it will be Season 6 before we see
any horror montages involving him and the

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:31.410
savoirs.

00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:32.950
Or maybe as a Season 5 finale cliffhanger
reveal.

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:37.590
I can understand the producers wanting to
wait to bring him out.

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:42.060
and my Number 1 pick for Negan - Bill Paxton

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:43.490
Hail Hydra, seriously.

00:07:43.490 --> 00:07:46.230
What’s the best part of Agents of SHIELD
right now.

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:47.760
Evil Bill Paxton.

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:51.760
Even though the writing on Kirman’s Walking
Dead books is totally different from the type

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:54.770
of things you see in a Marvel book it totally
works.

00:07:54.770 --> 00:07:58.600
Just a more sadistic version of the Garrett
character he’s playing right now.

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:02.580
And a lot more f-bombs casually dropped into
conversation.

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:07.320
Sometimes bigger actors like Paxton don’t
want to play villains back to back, but I

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:12.220
feel like he’s done so much with his Garrett
role, who’s essentially a C-List Marvel

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:13.220
character.

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:16.140
Think what he could do with someone like Negan.

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:20.850
The thing I like about Paxton is that he makes
you enjoy watching awful characters.

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:24.290
He’s so much fun to watch when he’s being
bad.

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:28.520
I think the big question we need to ask though
is what kind of a tone is the show going to

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:29.691
have when Negan does appear.

00:08:29.691 --> 00:08:30.990
Regardless of how long it takes.

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:34.550
Scott Gimple has been pretty clear that the
show season to season becomes a different

00:08:34.550 --> 00:08:35.550
show.

00:08:35.550 --> 00:08:38.560
Like Season 3 Walking Dead can be considered
a completely different show than Season 4

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:40.330
Walking Dead and so on.

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:45.510
Negan has a real comedic element to him that
the show is going to have to accomodate.

00:08:45.510 --> 00:08:49.680
And right now Walking Dead is definitely not
full of laughable moments.

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:53.220
The closest thing recently was when you got
Carl eating pudding on the roof.

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:57.790
And that was more of a moment of relief, not
laugh out loud funny.

00:08:57.790 --> 00:09:02.010
When Negan comes, I feel like we’re only
going to have two viable emotional responses.

00:09:02.010 --> 00:09:10.280
We can either laugh at him because he’s
so evil or we can cry because of the horrible

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:11.280
things he does.

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:13.440
I suppose you could try to do both.

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:17.370
But let me know who you’re favorite choice
to play Negan is.

00:09:17.370 --> 00:09:20.120
Like I said though, don’t expect him to
show up until at least the second half of

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:22.330
the season and even then only briefly.

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:27.080
So like I said, while I’m working on my
bonus video for next week write your suggestions

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:29.980
for other bonus Walking Dead vids in the comments.

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:36.800
I’ll try to make it a regular Thursday or
Friday thing.

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:42.100
Right now click here for my Season 5 predictions
and click here for my finale video.

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:43.790
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow.

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:44.760
High Fives!

